{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghW4WmrqYfPxphT5EWhw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Model.** For d⁷ in a tetrahedral field, the ground state is ⁴A₂(F). The three spin-allowed bands are:\n\n- ν₁ = ⁴T₂(F) ← ⁴A₂, with energy 10Dq.\n- ν₂ = ⁴T₁(F) ← ⁴A₂.\n- ν₃ = ⁴T₁(P) ← ⁴A₂.\n\nν₂ and ν₃ are the two roots of the 2×2 ⁴T₁ (F, P) configuration-interaction matrix, measured from the ground state. I wrote this matrix from memory, taking the d³ octahedral form with the same Dq. I did not check the off-diagonal term of 4B against a reference.\n\n| | ⁴T₁(F) | ⁴T₁(P) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ⁴T₁(F) | 18Dq | 4B |\n| ⁴T₁(P) | 4B | 15B + 6Dq |\n\n**Solving with ν₂ and ν₃.** The sum and product of the two roots give two equations:\n\n- Sum: 15B + 24Dq = 7520 + 18640 = 26 160.\n- Product: 18Dq(15B + 6Dq) − 16B² = 7520 × 18640 ≈ 1.4017×10⁸.\n\nFrom the sum, B = 1744 − 1.6Dq. Substituting into the product gives Dq² − 1535Dq + 5.17×10⁵ = 0. The roots are Dq ≈ 500 cm⁻¹ and Dq ≈ 1035 cm⁻¹.\n\nI took the lower root. The higher one gives B ≈ 90 cm⁻¹, which is unphysical. With Dq = 500, B = 1744 − 800 ≈ 944 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Check against ν₁.** Dq = 500 predicts ν₁ = 10Dq = 5000 cm⁻¹, but the observed band is 4330 cm⁻¹. Using ν₁ alone would give Dq ≈ 433 cm⁻¹. That value does not reproduce ν₂ and ν₃ in the matrix: it gives a product of about 1.25×10⁸ against 1.40×10⁸ observed. The data are therefore not fully self-consistent in this model. Possible causes are vibronic or spin–orbit effects, which the model ignores, or a misassigned band.\n\n**Result.** The best fit to ν₂ and ν₃ is Dq ≈ 500 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 940 cm⁻¹. This is about 97% of the free-ion B for Co²⁺ (≈ 970 cm⁻¹). The ν₁ mismatch of about 670 cm⁻¹ means Dq is uncertain by roughly ±10%.\n\nC cannot be determined from these three bands, so I have not reported it.\n\n{\"Dq\": 500, \"B\": 944, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Fit of nu2 and nu3 with the d7 Td 4T1(F)/(P) CI matrix; nu1 is not reproduced exactly (5000 vs 4330 cm-1) and C is not determinable from these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":795,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":795,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08887c9d-ff9a-45f7-8662-0b86e0a16fd5","uuid":"9fbbd051-3da6-4161-9c74-d1913fd31c07","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:35:16.045Z","request_id":"req_011CghW4WJaG2ZS88pz2cCe3"}
